# --- experiments/: one committed dir per run/experiment (code + seeds + small
# results), grouped by type {active_learning, oracle_validation, ablations}. Run
# OUTPUTS — timestamped run dirs (YYYY-MM-DD_*) and everything under them
# (checkpoints, logs, modes, per-round CSVs) — are regenerable and ignored by
# pattern; all committed code/seeds/results outside them stay tracked. ---
experiments/**/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]_*/
# committed seed + result CSVs sit directly in a run dir (override the global *.csv ignore)
!experiments/**/seed_*.csv
!experiments/**/*_results.csv

# ...but the two rules above key on FILE NAMING, and the lsd_hubs analyses never adopted that
# convention: their outputs are curve_hub_batching.csv, reaction_axis_ratio.csv, summary.csv,
# pipeline_headline.csv. So they fell through to the blanket `*.csv` and stayed invisible --
# 454 CSVs under experiments/lsd_hubs of which only 12 were tracked, including every headline
# artifact (reaction_axis_ratio.csv IS the 2.93x matrix result). Nobody noticed for months because
# `git add` NO-OPS SILENTLY on an ignored path; the failure mode is the silence, not the size.
#
# Un-ignore by LOCATION as well as by name. `results*/` is where analysis outputs already live by
# convention, so this states the rule the tree was already following.
#
# VERIFY BOTH DIRECTIONS when touching this. It is not enough that the files you want became
# trackable -- a representative bulk-data CSV must still be IGNORED, or this has quietly re-enabled
# committing docking dumps. Checked 2026-09-08: analysis outputs trackable, while
# experiments/lsd_hubs/campaign/enum_dump.csv and .../scale5k/analysis/*.csv still hit the blanket
# rule at the top of this file.
#
# Scope, measured: 454 CSVs / 12.4 MB, largest single file 0.5 MB. 450 sit under a results dir; the
# other 4 (matrix16/manifest*.csv, dropoff/funnel_*_results.csv) were already tracked, so the
# location rule is exactly sufficient. One file outside lsd_hubs is also exposed --
# aizynth_failure_modes/results/residual_taxonomy.csv -- an analysis result of the same class.
#
# THESE ARE ARCHIVAL, NOT A BASELINE. They are committed so the v1 record exists somewhere durable
# rather than only on this filesystem and the /project backups. benchmark_v2 owes them nothing: the
# point of the re-run is to leave the previous campaign in the past, and the two are not
# commensurable anyway (different training budget, hit gates, generator taxonomy and pipeline
# shape). Do not diff v1 against v2 and read the difference as a result.
!experiments/**/results*/**/*.csv

# benchmark_v2 gets ALL its CSVs, results dir or not: grid.csv (the cell list every driver reads)
# and PROVENANCE.csv (the only record of what was generated versus copied forward) sit at its root,
# and losing either would leave that tree unable to say what it contains -- the one thing it exists
# to guarantee. Both were silently dropped from its first commit by the blanket rule.
!experiments/benchmark_v2/**/*.csv

